Carafe: wine_nx_runtime_log_flush writes out what the runtime's log and the game's log still hold, and the card
writes held back with them. The overlay calls it before it lets the system close the game from the HOME Menu,
which ends the process before the next periodic flush: the last lines of the log were lost.
LGPL-2.1-or-later, as the file it changes.

--- a/horizon-wine/source/runtime.c
+++ b/horizon-wine/source/runtime.c
@@ -499,6 +499,15 @@
     log_line( "%s", msg );
 }
 
+void wine_nx_runtime_log_flush( void )
+{
+    pthread_mutex_lock( &log_mutex );
+    if (log_file) fflush( log_file );
+    if (game_log_file) fflush( game_log_file );
+    pthread_mutex_unlock( &log_mutex );
+    wine_nx_sd_cache_flush();
+}
+
